 "text": "Hey there, how are you? You can use a cable organizer that wraps around the back of a desk and keeps the cables on top. They' very effective. It' a small box that you loop the cables through, and it keeps them neatly on top of the desk. It stops them digging into the desk and making a nest. Not really. It's bit of a faff to do while you' moving, but it' worth it for years of peace. Some desks come with one built in, so check there first. Then maybe start there. Start at each end of the desk and push the cable through each time you sit down or stand. For the monitor cables, you can use little hooks that stick directly onto the back of the monitor. They' really neat.",
